cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Fullseye in academic work, please cite it as below."
title: "Fullseye: an explainable classical-vision operator library and workbench for Physical AI"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Furuse"
    given-names: "Kazufumi"
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.1.1
date-released: "2026-08-30"
abstract: >-
  Fullseye is a numpy-native library of ~1000 typed classical image-processing and
  geometric-vision operators (2-D and 3-D), with an evolutionary pipeline-design mode
  evaluated under honest held-out gates, a Physical-AI perception stack
  (stereo -> depth -> point cloud -> 6-DoF pose), and an HDevelop-style IDE
  (Fullseye Studio). Every operator carries a machine-readable Markdown note
  (contract, references, license, version fingerprint) designed to double as a
  retrieval corpus for AI assistants and as a reproducible, citable methods reference.
keywords:
  - image processing
  - machine vision
  - explainable algorithms
  - robotics perception
  - evolutionary computation
